*** src/FindSteps.maude — a `find` reduction, one arrow per equation, anywhere.
***
*** src/sem/Steps.maude recovers the paper's derivations by reflecting the
*** domain module and turning every equation whose left-hand side is a
*** CONFIGURATION into a rule, so that one `~>` is one statement. This file is
*** that construction one layer down: one `~>` is one equation of the storage
*** model, applied at whatever position it fires — INCLUDING inside the term.
*** It is what shows the copy leaf being built and then dispatched, and what
*** shows the sub-read that decides the leaf's left side, both of which a
*** statement-level derivation hides inside a single arrow.
***
***     red in PAPER-FIND-SORTED :
***         findSteps('PAPER-CMP-SORTED, find(s3, $ledger2 $nonce)) .
***
***     find(s3, $ledger2 $nonce)
***      ~> find(ovr(v→st(find(save(save(mtSt, $ledger $nonce, 5),     selectOnSaveCons:
***                              $ledger $balances 1, 11), $ledger2)),   the leaf,
***                 save(save(mtSt, $nonce, 5), $balances 1, 11)),       target-old
***              $nonce)                                                 still pending
***      ~> find(ovr(v→st(find(save(mtSt, $ledger $nonce, 5), $ledger2)), …), $nonce)
***      ~> find(ovr(v→st(find(mtSt, $ledger2)), …), $nonce)      target had nothing
***      ~> find(ovr(v→st(mtSt), …), $nonce)
***      ~> find(ovr(mtSt, save(save(mtSt, $nonce, 5), $balances 1, 11)), $nonce)
***      ~> find(save(save(mtSt, $nonce, 5), $balances 1, 11), $nonce)  ovr / PrimField:
***      ~> find(save(mtSt, $nonce, 5), $nonce)                           read RIGHT
***      ~> 5
***
*** The middle four arrows are the point. `find(s2, $ledger2)` under `v→st` is
*** the question "what did the TARGET hold before the copy?", and its answer is
*** what the mapping members will later be read from. An earlier version of this
*** file stepped only the OUTERMOST `find`, so all four collapsed into the first
*** arrow and the leaf appeared with its left side already computed.
***
*** The module to step is the first argument, a Qid, and the term to step is
*** the second. The constants the term is built from must be declared INSIDE
*** that module: one added from outside does not exist in the module
*** metaRewrite runs in, the same trap sem/Steps.maude records.
***
*** TWO MODULES, and the split matters. FIND-META holds META-LEVEL and the
*** metaprogram, and is NOT parameterized: the transformation reads a module
*** term and knows nothing about storage. FIND-TRACE{X :: STORAGE-API} is the
*** thin wrapper that has to mention `X$StValue`, and it takes the module to
*** step as a Qid argument rather than a `theModule` constant, so two instances
*** over two different storage models can sit in one file without racing to
*** define one constant. Instantiating FIND-TRACE therefore does not copy
*** META-LEVEL.
***
*** THE CONSTRUCTION. To see every step, `find` must not reduce at all — an
*** equational `find` normalizes its inner reads away before any outer rule can
*** fire. So in the clone:
***
***   1. `drop` DELETES every equation whose left-hand side is headed by `find`
***      or `v→st`. Those two symbols are now inert: a term keeps its shape.
***   2. `mkR` re-adds exactly those equations as RULES, left- and right-hand
***      sides unchanged — so a rule's right-hand side keeps its inner `find`s
***      steppable — and only the CONDITION rewritten.
***   3. `shadow` re-adds them a second time as EQUATIONS under the shadow names
***      `findE` / `vstE`, and `addE` / `shMb` give those names the same
***      profiles and membership axioms.
***
*** Step 3 is what makes the FLAGGED model work. StorageFlag's dispatch is
*** conditional — `ceq find(ovr(st, nd), f flds) = find(nd, f flds) if
*** isMap(find(st, f)) = false /\ prm := find(nd, f)` — and those conditions
*** call `find`. Rewritten to `findE`, they still reduce and still decide,
*** while the subject term's own `find`s stay frozen. With a single inert
*** `find` the guards could never decide and every trace would stall on the leaf.
***
*** INNERMOST-LEFTMOST, and it is not cosmetic. `stp` recurses into arguments
*** and steps at the top only when no argument can step. That order guarantees a
*** sub-read like `find(s2, $ledger2)` is resolved BEFORE the enclosing `ovr`
*** dispatch is attempted, so `isMap(findE(st, f))` always has a ground `st`.
*** Outermost order would attempt the dispatch against an unreduced left side.
***
*** TWO TRAPS THIS FILE PAID FOR
***
***   `_/\_` HAS `nil` AS ITS IDENTITY. The obvious condition traversal,
***   `eq renC(C1 /\ C2) = renC(C1) /\ renC(C2)`, matches ANY single condition
***   with C2 bound to nil, and loops forever. Peel one fragment at a time
***   instead, as `renC` below does.
***
***   DO NOT DEEP-RENAME THE FLATTENED MODULE. `upModule(Q, true)` drags in the
***   whole prelude; walking every term of every equation in it exhausts memory.
***   Only the `find` / `v→st` equations need renaming, and they are selected by
***   a head-level match that never looks inside anything else.
***
*** THE META-LEVEL TRAPS of Steps.maude apply unchanged, two of them here. The
*** LIST renamings keep META-LEVEL's NatList out of List{Field}'s kind, which
*** `Int < Field$Elt` would otherwise merge with. And a term cannot be held
*** as-is while it is stepped, since `find` would normalize it away in the
*** CALLER's module, where it is still equational: `inert` is the frozen
*** wrapper, `[strat (0)]`, uplifted whole and stripped at the meta level by
*** `stepT`. Do not give the wrapper a name containing `|` — `'~`|_`|~` does
*** not lex as a Qid literal. The wrapper is why a raw trace prints as
*** `inert(find(…)) ~> inert(find(…))`; the expected-value comments beside each
*** reduction drop it.
***
*** PRIORITY. `[owise]` is dropped when an equation becomes a rule, because
*** rules have no `owise`. The disjoint-path passthrough of the sorted model,
*** `ceq find(save(st, fldsN, val), fldsN2) = find(st, fldsN2) if fldsN =/=
*** fldsN2 [owise]`, therefore relies on coming last among the rules. It does,
*** but EquationSet is assoc comm, so that is an observation and not a
*** guarantee: pair every `findSteps` with a plain `red find(…) .`, and a
*** mis-ordered trace shows up as a final value that disagrees.

sload StorageApi .

fmod FIND-META is
    pr META-LEVEL * (sort Trace to MetaTrace,
        op _`[_`] : Qid NeTermList -> Term to _`{`[_`]`},
        op _+_ : ModuleExpression ModuleExpression -> ModuleExpression to _+M_,
        op nil : -> NatList to nilN,
        op __ : NatList NatList -> NatList to _;;_,
        op append : NatList NatList -> NatList to appendN,
        op head : NeNatList -> Nat to headN,
        op tail : NeNatList -> NatList to tailN,
        op last : NeNatList -> Nat to lastN,
        op front : NeNatList -> NatList to frontN,
        op occurs : Nat NatList -> Bool to occursN,
        op reverse : NatList -> NatList to reverseN,
        op $reverse : NatList NatList -> NatList to $reverseN,
        op size : NatList -> Nat to sizeN,
        op $size : NatList Nat -> Nat to $sizeN) .

    var H : Header .             var IL : ImportList .    var SS : SortSet .
    var SSDS : SubsortDeclSet .  var MAS : MembAxSet .    var MA : MembAx .
    var OPDS : OpDeclSet .       var OPD : OpDecl .
    var EQS : EquationSet .      var EQ : Equation .      var AS : AttrSet .
    vars T T2 : Term .           var NTL NTL2 : NeTermList .
    var COND : Condition .
    var TYL : TypeList .         var TY : Type .
    vars Q Qd : Qid .            var S : Sort .

    *** ---- deep rename, applied ONLY to the find / v→st equations ---------
    op ren : Term -> Term .
    op renL : NeTermList -> NeTermList .
    eq ren('find{[NTL]}) = 'findE{[renL(NTL)]} .
    eq ren('v→st{[NTL]}) = 'vstE{[renL(NTL)]} .
    ceq ren(Qd{[NTL]}) = Qd{[renL(NTL)]} if Qd =/= 'find /\ Qd =/= 'v→st .
    eq ren(T) = T [owise] .
    eq renL((T, NTL)) = (ren(T), renL(NTL)) .
    eq renL(T) = ren(T) .

    *** `_/\_` has nil as its IDENTITY, so peel one fragment at a time: a
    *** two-variable split would match every single condition with the second
    *** half bound to nil, and recur forever.
    op renC : Condition -> Condition .
    eq renC(nil) = nil .
    eq renC((T = T2)  /\ COND) = (ren(T) = ren(T2))  /\ renC(COND) .
    eq renC((T := T2) /\ COND) = (ren(T) := ren(T2)) /\ renC(COND) .
    eq renC((T : S)   /\ COND) = (ren(T) : S)        /\ renC(COND) .

    *** ---- 1. the stepped symbols lose their equations --------------------
    op drop : EquationSet -> EquationSet .
    eq drop(none) = none .
    eq drop((eq 'find{[NTL]} = T [AS] .) EQS) = drop(EQS) .
    eq drop((ceq 'find{[NTL]} = T if COND [AS] .) EQS) = drop(EQS) .
    eq drop((eq 'v→st{[NTL]} = T [AS] .) EQS) = drop(EQS) .
    eq drop((ceq 'v→st{[NTL]} = T if COND [AS] .) EQS) = drop(EQS) .
    eq drop(EQ EQS) = EQ drop(EQS) [owise] .

    *** ---- 2. and come back as rules, conditions shadowed ------------------
    op mkR : EquationSet -> RuleSet .
    eq mkR(none) = none .
    eq mkR((eq 'find{[NTL]} = T [AS] .) EQS) =
        (rl 'find{[NTL]} => T [label('fnd)] .) mkR(EQS) .
    eq mkR((ceq 'find{[NTL]} = T if COND [AS] .) EQS) =
        (crl 'find{[NTL]} => T if renC(COND) [label('fnd)] .) mkR(EQS) .
    eq mkR((eq 'v→st{[NTL]} = T [AS] .) EQS) =
        (rl 'v→st{[NTL]} => T [label('fnd)] .) mkR(EQS) .
    eq mkR((ceq 'v→st{[NTL]} = T if COND [AS] .) EQS) =
        (crl 'v→st{[NTL]} => T if renC(COND) [label('fnd)] .) mkR(EQS) .
    eq mkR(EQ EQS) = mkR(EQS) [owise] .

    *** ---- 3. and a second time as equations, for the conditions to call ---
    op shadow : EquationSet -> EquationSet .
    eq shadow(none) = none .
    eq shadow((eq 'find{[NTL]} = T [AS] .) EQS) =
        (eq ren('find{[NTL]}) = ren(T) [AS] .) shadow(EQS) .
    eq shadow((ceq 'find{[NTL]} = T if COND [AS] .) EQS) =
        (ceq ren('find{[NTL]}) = ren(T) if renC(COND) [AS] .) shadow(EQS) .
    eq shadow((eq 'v→st{[NTL]} = T [AS] .) EQS) =
        (eq ren('v→st{[NTL]}) = ren(T) [AS] .) shadow(EQS) .
    eq shadow((ceq 'v→st{[NTL]} = T if COND [AS] .) EQS) =
        (ceq ren('v→st{[NTL]}) = ren(T) if renC(COND) [AS] .) shadow(EQS) .
    eq shadow(EQ EQS) = shadow(EQS) [owise] .

    *** the shadow names need the same profiles, and the same memberships:
    *** StorageCopy stamps a symbolic read as a Struct with `mb find(…)`.
    op addE : OpDeclSet -> OpDeclSet .
    eq addE(none) = none .
    eq addE((op 'find : TYL -> TY [AS] .) OPDS) =
        (op 'find : TYL -> TY [AS] .) (op 'findE : TYL -> TY [none] .) addE(OPDS) .
    eq addE((op 'v→st : TYL -> TY [AS] .) OPDS) =
        (op 'v→st : TYL -> TY [AS] .) (op 'vstE : TYL -> TY [none] .) addE(OPDS) .
    eq addE(OPD OPDS) = OPD addE(OPDS) [owise] .

    op shMb : MembAxSet -> MembAxSet .
    eq shMb(none) = none .
    eq shMb((mb 'find{[NTL]} : S [AS] .) MAS) =
        (mb 'find{[NTL]} : S [AS] .) (mb ren('find{[NTL]}) : S [AS] .) shMb(MAS) .
    eq shMb(MA MAS) = MA shMb(MAS) [owise] .

    op findModule : Qid -> Module [memo] .
    eq findModule(Q) = mkMod(upModule(Q, true)) .
    op mkMod : Module -> Module .
    eq mkMod(fmod H is IL sorts SS . SSDS OPDS MAS EQS endfm) =
        (mod H is IL sorts SS . SSDS addE(OPDS) shMb(MAS)
            (drop(EQS) shadow(EQS)) mkR(EQS) endm) .

    *** ---- one step, innermost-leftmost -----------------------------------
    *** `find` and `v→st` are inert here, so metaRewrite normalizes only the
    *** surrounding helpers before applying exactly one rule at the top.
    op top1 : Qid Term -> Term .
    eq top1(Q, T) = getTerm(metaRewrite(findModule(Q), T, 1)) .

    op stp : Qid Term -> Term .
    op stpL : Qid NeTermList -> NeTermList .
    ceq stp(Q, 'find{[NTL]}) =
        if NTL2 =/= NTL then 'find{[NTL2]} else top1(Q, 'find{[NTL]}) fi
        if NTL2 := stpL(Q, NTL) .
    ceq stp(Q, 'v→st{[NTL]}) =
        if NTL2 =/= NTL then 'v→st{[NTL2]} else top1(Q, 'v→st{[NTL]}) fi
        if NTL2 := stpL(Q, NTL) .
    ceq stp(Q, Qd{[NTL]}) = Qd{[stpL(Q, NTL)]} if Qd =/= 'find /\ Qd =/= 'v→st .
    eq stp(Q, T) = T [owise] .
    ceq stpL(Q, (T, NTL)) = if T2 =/= T then (T2, NTL) else (T, stpL(Q, NTL)) fi
        if T2 := stp(Q, T) .
    eq stpL(Q, T) = stp(Q, T) .

    *** The argument arrives wrapped and frozen; unwrap, step, wrap again.
    op stepT : Qid Term -> Term .
    eq stepT(Q, 'inert{[T]}) = 'inert{[stp(Q, T)]} .
endfm

fmod FIND-TRACE{X :: STORAGE-API} is
    pr FIND-META .

    sorts FState FTrace .
    subsort FState < FTrace .
    *** frozen: the whole point is that this find does NOT reduce
    op inert : X$StValue -> FState [ctor strat (0)] .
    op bad : -> FState [ctor] .
    op _~>_ : FState FTrace -> FTrace [ctor prec 90 gather (e E)] .

    var Q : Qid .   var N : Nat .   var V : X$StValue .   vars FS FS2 : FState .

    op fstep : Qid FState -> FState .
    eq fstep(Q, inert(V)) = downTerm(stepT(Q, upTerm(inert(V))), bad) .
    eq fstep(Q, bad) = bad .

    *** `findSteps` is frozen too, or its argument is the answer before it is
    *** ever seen. The bound is a safety net; a storage read terminates.
    op findSteps : Qid X$StValue -> FTrace [strat (0 1)] .
    eq findSteps(Q, V) = ftr(Q, inert(V), 100) .

    op ftr : Qid FState Nat -> FTrace .
    eq ftr(Q, bad, N) = bad .
    eq ftr(Q, FS, 0) = FS .
    ceq ftr(Q, FS, s N) = if FS2 == FS then FS else (FS ~> ftr(Q, FS2, N)) fi
        if FS2 := fstep(Q, FS) .
endfm
